notes:
Submitted unvalidated in the closing minutes, on the reasoning that the server keeps the best
score so a bad submission costs only a round trip. It was NOT a bad submission: 118,401 -> 61,447,
a 1.93x gain that had been sitting on main unsubmitted, built by a parallel effort
("Reverse lists with parallel value carriers", commit f673408).

The lesson is the archive gap, not the grid. Three of our live scores today came from grids that
were never committed, and this is the mirror case — a grid that was committed and never submitted.
Both cost us. A grid is only banked when the score is on the board AND the generator is in the
repo; either half alone is a loss waiting to happen.

